# TestFlight observability (agent checklist)

After **`bun run ios:testflight`** completes and ASC shows **VALID**, run:

```bash
bun run ios:check-tf-feedback
bun run ios:check-asc-builds
```

| Command | Source | What it covers |
|---------|--------|----------------|
| `ios:check-tf-feedback` | ASC API + Luciq | Screenshot comments, crash submissions, Luciq app list / manual hint |
| `ios:check-asc-feedback` | ASC only | Same ASC half without Luciq |
| `ios:check-luciq` | Luciq dashboard API (optional) | Needs `LUCIQ_API_TOKEN` + `LUCIQ_ACCOUNT_EMAIL` in Doppler |

## Luciq SDK token (build time)

- Doppler `purple-life` / `prd`: **`LUCIQ_APP_TOKEN`** (SDK app token, never commit).
- Injected via `--dart-define=LUCIQ_APP_TOKEN=...` in `scripts/flutter-ios-testflight.sh`.
- Flutter init: `flutter/lib/core/observability/luciq_bootstrap.dart` (skips web + empty token).
- Dashboard project: **Flutter - Purple - Beta**.

## When testers report crashes

1. ASC `betaFeedbackCrashSubmissions` is often **empty** for screenshot-only reports.
2. Check Luciq **Crashes** and **App Health** (crashes upload on **next launch**).
3. Track open issue **`tf-crash-report`** in `docs/OPEN-ISSUES.md`.

## Alternatives (policy)

See `mem/observability/crash-reporting.md`. Luciq stays primary for TestFlight until
`tf-crash-report` is resolved or cost/policy triggers migration (Sentry, Crashlytics).
